## Stage the Compute Configuration

In stateful mode OpenHPC is added in the same provisioning pass as the base OS,
the xCAT-native way, rather than by logging in to the running nodes. Two things
are staged on the head node and applied automatically when a node installs:

- an **otherpkgs pkglist** -- the OpenHPC packages xCAT installs into the node,
  from the OpenHPC, EPEL, and CRB repositories named by `otherpkgdir`; and
- a **postscript** (`ohpc-config`) -- the configuration commands xCAT runs on the
  node at first boot, after those packages are installed.

The customization chapters later in this guide add to both through the same
compute macros used by every provisioner, so no step is xCAT-specific: a package
step appends a name to the pkglist, and a configuration step appends a shell
command to the postscript. Both files are created fresh here, so re-running the
guide from the top does not accumulate duplicate entries.

The postscript is an ordinary shell script that xCAT runs on each node the first
time it is provisioned. Its commands append to and edit node files directly, so
they are written to apply cleanly on a freshly installed node -- but they are not
de-duplicated. Re-applying the postscript to an already-configured node (for
example with `updatenode -P`, or by enabling `runbootscripts`) can therefore add
duplicate lines; review the assembled script before provisioning (see the deploy
chapter) and adjust it for such uses.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Stage OpenHPC package list and configuration postscript -->
```bash
# Locations of the staged package list and configuration postscript. The macros
# in the customization chapters append to these (via ${OHPC_OTHERPKGS} and
# ${OHPC_POSTSCRIPT}); xCAT applies them when the node is provisioned.
OHPC_OTHERPKGS=/install/custom/install/{{ distro }}/ohpc.otherpkgs.pkglist
OHPC_POSTSCRIPT=/install/postscripts/{{ xcat_config_postscript | default("ohpc-config") }}
export OHPC_OTHERPKGS OHPC_POSTSCRIPT

# OpenHPC packages to install on the compute nodes (created fresh; the
# customization chapters append to this list).
mkdir -p "$(dirname "${OHPC_OTHERPKGS}")"
cat > "${OHPC_OTHERPKGS}" << 'EOF'
ohpc-base-compute
ohpc-slurm-client
lmod-ohpc
chrony
nfs-utils
EOF

# OpenHPC, EPEL, and CRB repositories that provide the packages above. The base
# OS repositories are served from the head node's /install tree automatically.
chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} \
    otherpkglist="${OHPC_OTHERPKGS}" \
    otherpkgdir="{{ ohpc_repo_server }}/OpenHPC/{{ ohpc_version_tree }}/{{ ostree }}/,\
{{ epel_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/Everything/{{ arch }}/,\
{{ distro_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/CRB/{{ arch }}/os/"

# Compute configuration postscript (created fresh with a shebang; the
# customization chapters append commands). xCAT runs it on each node at first
# boot, after the OpenHPC packages above are installed. ${sms_ip} is expanded
# here, as the head writes the file.
cat > "${OHPC_POSTSCRIPT}" << EOF
#!/bin/sh
# OpenHPC compute configuration -- generated by the install recipe, run by xCAT.
systemctl disable --now firewalld
# Register the Slurm server with the computes (configless mode)
echo SLURMD_OPTIONS="--conf-server ${sms_ip}" > /etc/sysconfig/slurmd
# Point time synchronization at the head node
echo "server ${sms_ip} iburst" >> /etc/chrony.conf
# NFS client mounts of /home and the OpenHPC public tree
echo "${sms_ip}:/home /home nfs nfsvers=4,nodev,nosuid 0 0" >> /etc/fstab
echo "${sms_ip}:/opt/ohpc/pub /opt/ohpc/pub nfs nfsvers=4,nodev 0 0" >> /etc/fstab
mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/pub
mount -a
# Enable and start services now. The postscript runs at first boot after the
# packages are installed, and there is no further reboot, so use --now to both
# enable-on-boot and start immediately; otherwise the node comes up with munge
# and slurmd inactive and never registers with the controller.
systemctl enable --now munge
systemctl enable --now slurmd
systemctl enable --now chronyd
EOF
chmod 0755 "${OHPC_POSTSCRIPT}"

# Run the postscript on every compute node at provisioning (after the default
# otherpkgs postbootscript, so the packages it configures are present).
chdef compute -p postbootscripts={{ xcat_config_postscript | default("ohpc-config") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

The head node exports `/home` and `/opt/ohpc/pub`; disable the xCAT-managed
`/tftpboot` and `/install` export entries so they do not conflict:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Adjust head node NFS exports for the compute mounts -->
```bash
perl -pi -e "s|/tftpboot|#/tftpboot|" /etc/exports
perl -pi -e "s|/install|#/install|"   /etc/exports
exportfs -a
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
